Condition : 20 - Before each phase of the development hereby approved is first occupied or brought into use, an updated Parking Management Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Plan shall include the following:
(a) details of parking allocations of the approved development and how this will be operated and enforced ;
(b) details of measures proposed to restrict parking to designated bays only and prohibit parking on the access road;
(c) a commitment to convert passive EV bays to active and to provide additional Blue Badge bays when demand requires;
(d) details of the operation of any gates or barriers, signage, road marking, and any other road safety measures adopted on site;
(e) details of car club/ car sharing facilities and how this will be managed;
(f) details of how parking will be monitored and managed during shift changeovers;
(g) measures to ensure that all prospective occupiers are informed of the Parking Management Plan.
The parking areas and access road(s) shall thereafter be managed in compliance with the approved details, unless the prior written approval of the local planning authority is obtained to secure any variation.
Reason: In order to promote sustainable modes of transport, to protect neighbours' living conditions and to ensure minimal disruption of traffic in the locality.

Condition : 26 - Notwithstanding any details included in the submitted plans, no development above ground level (except any demolition, site clearance, ground investigation and remediation work) shall take place until details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. These details shall include:
a) a statement setting out the design objectives and how these will be delivered;
b) access and circulation areas, materials, means of enclosure/boundary treatment(s) and retaining structures;
c) minor artefacts and structures (e.g. furniture, refuse or other storage units, signs, lighting, renewable energy installations, CCTV, indicative services layout, etc., where relevant);
d) retained historic or other landscape features and proposals for restoration, where relevant;
e) planting plans, written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment); schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers and densities where appropriate; and
f) an implementation programme (including phasing of work where relevant).
The landscaping works shall comply with the requirements specified in BS 3936 (1992) 'Specification of Nursery Stock Part 1 Trees and Shrubs', and in BS 4428 (1989) 'Recommendations for General Landscape Operations', and shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, or such other date(s) as may be specified in the agreed implementation programme.
The trees that are hereby approved to be retained shall be protected before commencement of any works on site and throughout the course of the development by methods that conform to the best practice guidance contained in British Standard BS5837: 2012 or any guidance that shall have superseded it.
